    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0354" n="344" xml:id="pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/685</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Legation to the Department of State
                        </hi><anchor n="31" xml:id="d367-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>According to information received by the Governor General of the Netherlands East
                    Indies a Japanese Expeditionary Force has arrived in the vicinity of Palao.</p>
                <p>Should this force, [which is]<anchor n="32" xml:id="d367-f2"/> strong enough to
                    form a threat for the Netherlands East Indies or for Portuguese Timor, move
                    beyond a line between following points: Davao–Waigeo–Equator, the Governor
                    General will regard this as an act of aggression and will under those
                    circumstances consider the hostilities opened and act accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-21">November 21,
                            1941</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="31" type="source" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
                <p>Handed on November 21 to the Adviser on Political Relations (Hornbeck) by the
                    Netherland Minister (Loudon); noted by the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d367-f2" n="32" xml:id="d367-f2-content">
                <p>The bracketed words were inserted by Dr. Hornbeck with the following notation:
                    “Mr. Loudon stated that his telegram contained this affirmation.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
